## 4. Phase 4 — Verification Gate, Sanitization & Workflows
Before signaling task completion:
1. Pre-Commit Sanitization: Purge all debug prints (`console.log`, `print()`, `debugger;`), delete temporary scratch files (`git status` clean), eliminate dead imports.
2. Run type checker (`tsc`, `mypy`, `cargo check`).
3. Run linter (`eslint`, `ruff`, `cargo clippy`).
4. Run automated tests (`npm test`, `pytest`, `cargo test`).
5. Reconcile final git diff against acceptance criteria.
6. Provide evidence-based summary in your response.
7. Git != Versioning: Maintain the Bisect Invariant (every commit builds & passes). Use context-appropriate versioning (SemVer/CalVer/ZeroVer/Continuous). Avoid premature `@deprecated` in pre-1.0; separate technical `CHANGELOG.md` from user release notes.

